  ## What was built

  **Files changed (all under `bench/`, two commits on `gauntlet/bench`):**

  - `bench/run.sh` — the runner (`--agent`, `--tasks`, `--timeout`, `--runs`, `--out`, `--verify-fixtures`). Copies `repo/` to a fresh work dir per run, commits a base, runs the adapter with a timeout (uses `gtimeout` when present, a background watchdog otherwise), copies `hidden/` in only after the agent exits, runs `check.sh`, and records pass/fail, wall seconds, exit code, timeouts, `git diff --shortstat` vs base, and per-run logs under `bench/results/<timestamp>/`. Ends with a table plus pass rate, median and p90 wall time, and writes JSON.
  - `bench/agents/` — `noop.sh`, `reference.sh` (applies the patch found via `BENCH_TASK_DIR`), `codex.sh`, `fx.sh`, `slag-fix.sh` (placeholder with a TODO that the `slag fix` interface may change).
  - `bench/issues/` — 8 tasks, each with `repo/`, `ISSUE.md`, `hidden/`, `check.sh`, `reference.patch`, `meta.json`:
    - `py-passcheck` (easy): strength check uses OR instead of AND.
    - `py-invoice-dates` (medium): `add_months` crashes on year rollover and short months.
    - `py-pricetag-cache` (hard): price cache never invalidated; symptom shows up as wrong order totals in a different file.
    - `js-leaderboard` (easy): default string `sort()` on numeric points.
    - `js-user-pager` (medium): 0-based offset slip in `paginate.js` plus floor-instead-of-ceil in `api.js`.
    - `js-notify-preview` (medium): UTF-16 slicing splits surrogate pairs and counts emoji double.
    - `rust-hawkconf` (hard): lexer eats comment-ending newlines without bumping the line counter, so parse errors from `parser.rs` report wrong lines.
    - `sh-backup-rotate` (easy): rotation pipes the newest-first listing into `head` instead of skipping the kept prefix, deleting the newest backups.
  - `bench/regen-patches.sh` — maintainer tool that regenerates `reference.patch` files.
  - `bench/README.md`, `bench/.gitignore` (ignores timestamped run dirs, keeps `baseline-codex.json`).
  - `bench/results/baseline-codex.json` — the measured baseline.

  Hidden tests live outside `repo/` everywhere; every `ISSUE.md` is symptom-only prose. Visible suites pass on the buggy code; hidden suites fail on it and pass on the reference fix.

