• Leaks fixed, verified, and committed as `d31e974 bench: stop leaking hidden tests and reference patches to adapters, add leak check`.

  ## What changed

  - `bench/run.sh`
    - No longer passes `$task_dir/ISSUE.md` to adapters. New `prepare_issue_copy()` copies ISSUE.md into a fresh `mktemp -d` dir holding nothing else; the adapter gets that copy and the runner removes the temp dir after the run.
    - No longer exports `BENCH_TASK_DIR`. The runner sets `BENCH_REFERENCE_PATCH` only when `basename "$AGENT"` is `reference.sh`, and unsets it (plus any inherited `BENCH_TASK_DIR`) otherwise, so no other adapter sees a path into `bench/issues/`.
    - New `--leak-check` mode, and `--verify-fixtures` now runs the leak check first.
  - `bench/agents/reference.sh` — now reads `BENCH_REFERENCE_PATCH` instead of `BENCH_TASK_DIR`.
  - `bench/agents/probe.sh` — new probe adapter. It inspects `env` for `hidden` / `reference.patch` / `bench/issues`, checks the issue-file and repo-dir path strings, and lists the entries of the runner-controlled dirs (issue dir, repo dir, repo parent). Any hit fails the run. One perf note: my first version forked `basename` per entry across every ancestor dir up to `/`, which took 88s on the crowded `$TMPDIR`; the committed version checks path strings for ancestors and lists entries only in the three relevant dirs (0.2s).
  - `bench/README.md` — adapter contract and instrument-checks sections updated to match.

  Probe sanity: pointed at the old layout (`bench/issues/py-passcheck/ISSUE.md`) it reports all three leaks and exits 1.

